# Git stores text with LF, and every blob in this repo's history is LF. During
# the 3.5.0 work something rewrote 23 tracked files in the working tree to
# CRLF - no content change at all, but a diff of roughly 38,000 lines covering
# all of package-lock.json, the whole native plugin and every Xcode file. It
# was normalised back by hand. This stops the next editor, sync client or tool
# from doing it again, and makes `git status` stay quiet when one tries.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell and CI scripts break outright with CRLF, so they are named explicitly
# rather than left to auto-detection.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Never normalised. SVG is XML and is deliberately absent - it is text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Carried over from the 3.5.0 release branch during the frontier go
# reorientation. The CRLF problem it prevents is a property of this machine and
# this checkout, not of the product, so it survives the product change.
